{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "note": "What each kind of land unit needs: its profile, rig route, HOI4 animation roles, the Meshy library clips for each role, the entity states that play them, and the bones an entity attaches to. A job names one type with `unit_type`. Library clips are [action_id, key] pairs read from meshy_list_animations on 2026-11-05; the runner looks the ids up again (free) and refuses a clip whose key changed. `_inplace` clips have no root motion, so the unit does not slide. `body` names the type's body preset in body_presets.json, which measure_body.py checks against the measured generation.",
  "engine_limits": {
    "max_bones_per_skinned_mesh": 50,
    "max_influences_per_vertex": 4,
    "source": "gfx/FX/pdxmesh.shader of the installed game: `float4x4 matBones[50]` and `PDXMESH_MAX_INFLUENCE = 4` [vanilla-confirmed 1.19.4.1]"
  },
